# Trivy IaC scan suppressions.
# Each entry must carry an expiry date — no silent forever-suppressions.
# Format: AVD-XXX-XXXX exp:YYYY-MM-DD reason:<one line>
#
# Example:
# AVD-AWS-0123 exp:2026-12-31 reason:false positive in node-bootstrap vendor_data template

AVD-AWS-0104 exp:2027-07-07 reason:the egress rules of the cluster and node security groups in aws-control-plane: the destinations (registry_mirror_url, gitops_*_repo_url) are consumer-supplied and arbitrary, not enumerable at plan time or stable enough to CIDR-scope (CDN-backed hosts). This check only inspects CIDR breadth, not port, so port-scoping cannot clear it. Genuine domain-based egress restriction requires a separate network-layer control (NAT + firewall with FQDN allowlisting) that this module deliberately does not create — this project's modules never create network fabric. Unrestricted egress is also the AWS default security-group behavior.
